config-connector-extensions patch 0031: mockgcp's packet mirroring rules of a global network firewall policy: addPacketMirroringRule, getPacketMirroringRule, patchPacketMirroringRule, removePacketMirroringRule.

For compute.gcp.hfl.dev ComputeNetworkFirewallPolicyPacketMirroringRule.
Written here (upstream's mock answers Unimplemented; the HTTP routes are
generated already), after the policy's firewall rules in
networkfirewallpolicies.go: a rule is addressed by its priority in the
policy's packetMirroringRules; add refuses a rule without a priority or
at a priority the policy has; get, patch and remove answer 400 "The
firewall policy does not contain a packet mirroring rule at priority N"
for a priority it has not (modelled on the firewall rules' answer); a
patch replaces the rule whole; kind compute#packetMirroringRule;
tlsInspect is refused, even false, as the real API refused it in a live
run. No default rules are added and nothing else in the rule is
checked. A new file,
so it touches no file another patch edits.
diff --git a/mockgcp/mockcompute/networkfirewallpolicypacketmirroringrules.go b/mockgcp/mockcompute/networkfirewallpolicypacketmirroringrules.go
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..e9f3669e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/mockgcp/mockcompute/networkfirewallpolicypacketmirroringrules.go
@@ -0,0 +1,168 @@
